      body:
        "**When do you use the preterite?** For a **completed action** at a **definite time** in the past: *Ayer visité a mi abuela.* (Yesterday I visited my grandmother.) It's the tense of 'I did', 'she went', 'we played' — the events of a story.\n\n**How to form it (-ar verbs):** take the infinitive, remove *-ar* to find the stem, and add the preterite endings.\n\n| | hablar (to speak) | escuchar (to listen) |\n|---|---|---|\n| yo | habl**é** | escuch**é** |\n| tú | habl**aste** | escuch**aste** |\n| él / ella | habl**ó** | escuch**ó** |\n| nosotros / nosotras | habl**amos** | escuch**amos** |\n| vosotros / vosotras | habl**asteis** | escuch**asteis** |\n| ellos / ellas | habl**aron** | escuch**aron** |\n\n**Useful -ar verbs for your weekend, chores and trips** (*yo* form):\n\n| Spanish | English |\n|---|---|\n| visité a mi abuela | I visited my grandmother |\n| bailé en la fiesta | I danced at the party |\n| nadé en la piscina | I swam in the pool |\n| compré una camiseta | I bought a T-shirt |\n| escuché música | I listened to music |\n| cociné una paella de verduras | I cooked a vegetable paella |\n| limpié mi dormitorio | I cleaned my bedroom |\n| lavé los platos | I washed the dishes |\n| ayudé a mi madre | I helped my mother |\n| monté en bici | I rode my bike |\n| tomé el MRT | I took the MRT |\n| viajé a Málaga | I travelled to Málaga |\n| descansé | I rested |\n\n> **Accent alert.** Only the *yo* and *él / ella* forms carry an accent: *hablé, habló*. Compare *hablo* (I speak — present) with *habló* (he / she spoke — past). Forget the accent and you've changed the meaning.\n\n**Three more things to notice:**\n- The *tú* form ends in *-aste* — there is **no** *s* on the end: *hablaste*, not ~~hablastes~~.\n- The *nosotros* form is **the same as the present**: *hablamos* = 'we speak' or 'we spoke'. The context or a time phrase tells you which: *Ayer hablamos con Diego* (past) vs *Normalmente hablamos inglés en casa* (present).\n- Boot (stem-changing) *-ar* verbs **lose the boot** in the preterite: *pensar* → *pensé* (not ~~piensé~~), *despertarse* → *me desperté*, *acostarse* → *me acosté*.\n\n**Reflexive verbs** work in exactly the same way — the pronoun stays in front:\n\n    Me levanté a las siete, me duché y desayuné.\n    Mi hermano se levantó tarde.\n\n**Weather in the past:** *nevar* is an -ar verb, so 'it snowed' is *nevó*: *El año pasado nevó en Madrid.*",
